# AI Interaction Guidelines

## Project Context
You are working on a collection of AI-powered tools:
1. AI Writer: Text generation with style customization
2. Content Summarizer: URL and PDF content analysis
3. Code Explainer: Code analysis and documentation

## Code Generation Guidelines

### Frontend Components
- Generate responsive React components using Tailwind CSS
- Include proper TypeScript types and interfaces
- Implement error boundaries and loading states
- Add JSDoc comments for component props

### Backend Endpoints
- Follow RESTful API design patterns
- Include input validation and error handling
- Add Swagger/OpenAPI documentation
- Implement proper logging

### AI Integration
- Use streaming responses for real-time feedback
- Implement proper error handling for AI failures
- Add retry mechanisms for API calls
- Cache responses when appropriate

## Documentation Requirements
- Include clear component descriptions
- Document all props and return types
- Add usage examples
- Specify any dependencies or requirements

## Example Component Structure
```typescript
/**
 * A component that displays and processes user input
 * @param {string} initialValue - The initial input value
 * @param {(value: string) => void} onChange - Callback when input changes
 * @param {boolean} isProcessing - Whether the input is being processed
 */
interface InputProps {
  initialValue: string;
  onChange: (value: string) => void;
  isProcessing?: boolean;
}
```

## Testing Requirements
- Generate unit tests for utilities
- Include integration tests for API endpoints
- Add snapshot tests for components
- Test error handling and edge cases
